# ===========================================================================
#  .gitattributes -- line endings are decided here, not by whoever edited last
# ===========================================================================
#
#  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
#  This repository is written from a Windows machine and runs on Linux
#  servers. Three times an editor on the Windows side rewrote a whole file
#  with CRLF line endings, and each time the damage was quiet:
#
#    - a thirty-line change to miner/src/stratum.h arrived as a 1097-line
#      diff, which is a diff nobody can review
#    - scripts/gen_founder_key.py, the script that generates the founder's
#      key from a live USB, carried a shebang ending in a carriage return.
#      Run as ./scripts/gen_founder_key.py it answers "bad interpreter" --
#      at the one moment its operator is alone in front of a machine with
#      no second chance
#    - shell scripts on the servers had already broken this way once
#
#  core.autocrlf is a per-machine setting; it protects whoever set it and
#  nobody else. This file travels with the repository, so every clone and
#  every contributor gets the same answer.
#
#  scripts/test/test_line_endings.sh enforces it, because a rule that is
#  never checked is a preference.
# ===========================================================================

# Everything git recognises as text is stored and checked out with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Said explicitly for the file types that break rather than merely look odd.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.h         text eol=lf
*.cpp       text eol=lf
*.js        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.html      text eol=lf
*.css       text eol=lf
*.xml       text eol=lf
*.svg       text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
Makefile*   text eol=lf

# Binaries: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.gz        binary
*.tar       binary
*.zip       binary
*.tar.gz    binary
